  "timing_semantics_and_missing_evidence": [
    "requests.get(timeout=scalar) is not an end-to-end fetch-and-parse deadline. Completed source elapsed includes HTTP acquisition plus feedparser.parse; matching after the worker returns is outside that per-source measurement. Source durations cannot be summed to wall time because4workers overlap.",
    "The first4W01 extended completions took1.337-1.938s although their HTTP timeout parameter was about0.700s. Saved evidence cannot divide that into DNS/connect/read/redirect/decode/parse time or establish which component dominated.",
    "The pending4extended records set timed_out=true because the coordinator deadline elapsed, not because an HTTP timeout exception was observed. future.cancel() cannot cancel already-running work, and shutdown(wait=False) does not establish worker completion.",
    "Adapter timing starts after candidate/source preprocessing and ends before evidence enrichment. Service cache read/write, service merge, scanner interpretation, initial cache-only lookup and inter-call overhead are excluded from the reported sum. A single encompassing monotonic timer was not retained.",
    "No saved raw response bodies, final URLs, status/content-type for successful responses, feed version/bozo/entry counts, publication-rejection counts, issuer alias inputs, source phase timestamps, or post-return worker completion measurements exist in these artifacts. Available/0matches is insufficient to distinguish valid empty feed, stale/nonmatching feed or non-feed parse."
